Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:40:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(tofu): user_data is RequiresReplace -- any input change
 replaces the server

The UpCloud provider marks upcloud_server.user_data as RequiresReplace,
and every module input is rendered into it. So the documented
staging->production flip and the api_token_count rotation both destroy
and recreate the host (most likely with new IPs), rather than updating
it in place as the README claimed. Document that, recommend setting
acme_directory to its final value from the first apply, and explain how
cold-start ACME retries (5-minute timeout + Restart=on-failure) cover
the window before DNS points at the new host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
